{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run an LDAP directory on node1 for dc=branch,dc=test and import the staged identities and mail addresses unchanged.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The staged LDIF defines the required base and the alex and sam entries. Direct database and LDAP queries show both entries with their supplied names and mail addresses, including after node1 restarted.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b34921043cec4b6a","cmd-3e46733b7965496c","cmd-26db3d01913f418e"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Node2 can search the people subtree and find both users.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Searches issued from node2 returned exactly alex and sam with their expected attributes before and after both node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-02c05b49b0b1469b","cmd-0981078c04734fcc","cmd-b3ed55a400ec4d40"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Directory updates require an authenticated administrator, and anonymous writes fail.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Anonymous modifications were rejected with authentication-required errors. Authenticated administrator modifications succeeded, were read back, and were then reverted; the behavior was reconfirmed after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d76b45898f244cc8","cmd-d4a26581cef34b7d","cmd-831d6a3b4e39426a","cmd-8afbfae02d084239"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Preserve the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both nodes remained on CentOS 5.11 with kernel 2.6.18-398.el5. The installed LDAP packages are CentOS 5 builds, and the release and kernel remained unchanged after the required restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f308215778044a9d","cmd-4a41da72e84c4965","cmd-f7b65d60e6ae4f58","cmd-d5135765ca96459d","cmd-3055c180fa8e40ff","cmd-b3ed55a400ec4d40","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]}],"confidence":0.96,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"Task-related mutations were appropriately scoped: legacy-compatible package installation, LDAP configuration/import, boot enablement, and a node2-only firewall exception all directly supported the requested outcomes. Authentication-test writes were bounded and reverted. Two low-impact hygiene issues remain: the reboot commands left /tmp/ldap-reboot-node1.log and /tmp/ldap-reboot-node2.log, confirmed by final lifecycle observations; repository backup files named CentOS-Vault.repo.pre-ldap were created on both nodes and no later cleanup is shown, so they likely remained. The persistent repository URL changes themselves were justified prerequisites for installing compatible packages. Earlier non-sudo repository attempts failed at the initial copy and provide no evidence of mutation.","evidence_ids":["cmd-915c0be11a6c470f","cmd-380ec51ae0534238","cmd-66dbd067c944486f","cmd-62183ed8e9fd496f","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct functional evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol was also completed on both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity independently corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service/client and directory-search behavior. Only minor cleanup residue and limitations in the generic lifecycle probes reduce hygiene and confidence.","limitations":["The final generic listening-sockets observations are empty even though direct post-restart checks show slapd listening and node2 successfully querying it; the generic observation therefore does not independently corroborate socket state (cmd-26db3d01913f418e, cmd-b3ed55a400ec4d40, global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets).","The lifecycle package-health probe invoked an unsupported yum operation and could not establish overall package consistency, although both package transactions completed successfully.","The final evidence does not re-hash the staged LDIF file itself; preservation of the required identities and mail addresses is established by comparing its captured contents with direct post-import and post-restart directory results.","The repository backup files were not covered by the lifecycle inventory, so their continued presence is inferred from their creation and the absence of a cleanup command rather than directly observed."]}
